James wrote:

> How difficult would it be to code a new type of amnesia that times out, like
> hallucination? A MMF attack could still make you forget 25% of your
> items/maps, but that knowledge would gradually return over a period of time
> (which starts at, say, 1000 turns, and is doubled with each successful mind
> flaying).

Not difficult at all:

Add a field to the objclass that can record the turn number when you 
will regain the knowledge and initialize this field to 0 for all itemtypes.
When subject to amnesia add the timeout value to the turn counter 
(monstermoves) and record that into the objclass for those itemtypes 
that fall under the amnesia effect.
If re-identified clear the timeout.
In the main loop check through the itemtype database and return 
knowledge and clear the timeout of all itemtypes that has the current 
turn counter as their timeout.

Cost on processing speed: Whole itemtype database is searched wholly 
every turn (monstermoves).

The turn counter is monster moves as the player might get free turns.

